  "texSource": "%!TEX TS-program = xelatex\n% !BIB program = biber\n\\documentclass{article}[12pt]\n\\usepackage{setspace}\n\\singlespacing\n\\usepackage{ifpdf}\n\\usepackage{fontspec}\n\\usepackage[margin=0.75in]{geometry}\n\\usepackage{amsthm, amsmath, amssymb}\n\\usepackage[linguistics]{forest}\n\\usepackage{adjustbox}\n\\usepackage[loose,nice]{units}\n\\usepackage{tipa}\n\\usepackage{graphicx}\n\\usepackage{covington}\n\\usepackage{gb4e}\n\\noautomath\n\\let\\eachwordone=\\normalfont\n\\let\\eachwordone=\\textbf\n\\usepackage{hanging}\n\\usepackage{textgreek}\n\\usepackage{multirow}\n\\usepackage{multicol}\n\\setlength{\\multicolsep}{0pt}\n\\usepackage[normalem]{ulem}\n\\usepackage{stmaryrd}\n\\usepackage{hyperref}\n\\usepackage[backend=biber,style=unified,citestyle=authoryear-comp,maxcitenames=3,maxbibnames=99]{biblatex}\n\\DeclareFieldFormat{postnote}{#1}\n\\renewcommand{\\postnotedelim}{\\addcolon\\space}\n\\usepackage[utf8x]{inputenc}\n\n\\title{\\textbf{Beowulf: Prologue (Lines 1–11)}}\n\\author{Translated and glossed by Anonymous (Nowell Codex)}\n\\date{September 30, 2026}\n\n\\addbibresource{Voyages_of_Ohthere_Wulfstan.bib}\n\n\\begin{document}\n\\maketitle\n\n\\section{Text}\n\n\\begin{exe}\n\\ex \\label{ex:paragraph.1} \\begin{xlist}\n\n\\ex{\\gll Hwæt! Wē Gār-Dena in ġeār-dagum,\\\\\nhwā wē gārdena in ġeārdagum\\\\\n\\glt `Listen! We of the Spear-Danes in days of yore,'}\n\n\\ex{\\gll þēod-cyninga, þrym ġefrūnon,\\\\\nþēodcyninga þrym ġefrūnon\\\\\n\\glt `of the people's kings, have heard of their glory,'}\n\n\\ex{\\gll hū ðā æþelingas ellen fremedon.\\\\\nhū sē æþelingas ellen fremedon\\\\\n\\glt `how those noble princes performed courageous deeds.'}\n\n\\ex{\\gll Oft Scyld Scēfing sceaþena þrēatum,\\\\\noft scyld scēfing sceaþena þrēatum\\\\\n\\glt `Often Scyld Scefing from troops of enemies,'}\n\n\\ex{\\gll monegum mǣġþum, meodo-setla oftēah,\\\\\nmonegum mǣġþum meodosetla oftēah\\\\\n\\glt `from many tribes, seized the mead-benches,'}\n\n\\ex{\\gll egsode eorlas, syððan ǣrest wearð\\\\\negsode eorlas syððan ǣrest wearð\\\\\n\\glt `terrified the earls, after he was first'}\n\n\\ex{\\gll fēasceaft funden; hē þæs frōfre ġebād,\\\\\nfēasceaft funden hē sē frōfre ġebād\\\\\n\\glt `found destitute; he experienced solace for that,'}\n\n\\ex{\\gll wēox under wolcnum, weorðmyndum þāh,\\\\\nweaxan under wolcnum weorðmyndum þāh\\\\\n\\glt `grew under the clouds, prospered in honors,'}\n\n\\ex{\\gll oðþæt him ǣġhwylċ þāra ymbsittendra\\\\\noðþæt hē ǣġhwylċ sē ymbsittendra\\\\\n\\glt `until each of the surrounding peoples'}\n\n\\ex{\\gll ofer hron-rāde hȳran scolde,\\\\\nofer hronrāde hȳran scolde\\\\\n\\glt `across the whale-road had to obey him,'}\n\n\\ex{\\gll gomban gyldan. Þæt wæs gōd cyning!\\\\\ngomban gyldan sē wesan gōd cyning\\\\\n\\glt `and pay tribute. That was a good king!'}\n\n\\end{xlist}\n\\end{exe}\n\n\\end{document}\n"
